[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   Step 159 -- Perihelion-time leg-slip channel on the independent
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   refit record.
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   The transit anomaly has so far been measured in angle: the inbound-
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   and outbound-leg boundary asymptotes disagree (ddirf / d_in_leg), and
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   the catalogue leg rotation converts to an effective proper-time slip
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   through om_b = h/R^2 (step 065).  A conformal-lapse crossing is, at
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   root, a *timing* event -- the leg disagreement should therefore also
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   express directly as a perihelion-epoch discrepancy between orbit
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   solutions fitted independently to the pre- and post-perihelion arcs.
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   This step extracts that channel.  Each comet's two independent leg
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   fits (step_127 machinery on raw MPC astrometry, REBOUND/IAS15 +
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   DE440s, MAD clip) are re-derived on the cached observation record --
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   identical inputs, so the fits are deterministic reproductions -- and
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   each fitted leg state is converted to its osculating perihelion epoch
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   through a Keplerian two-body reduction anchored at the leg mid-epoch:
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   tp_leg = et_leg - M0 / n ,  n = sqrt(mu / |a|^3)
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   The boundary products (theta, ddirf, d_in_leg, cross-arc rms) are
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   joined from the step_b91 checkpoint rather than recomputed, since the
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   timing channel needs only the leg states.  The catalogue-side
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   companions (dtau, drot) come from step_b84.
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   Registered tests
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   T1  validity: per-comet |dtp_io| (inbound minus outbound osculating
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   perihelion epoch) must correlate with the catalogue slip |dtau|
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   and with our own leg disagreement ddirf -- both are projections
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   of the same non-closure, so concordance certifies the channel.
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   T2  cap contrast of |dtp_io| at the declared 60-deg cap on the
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   independent theta, MWU + label-shuffle permutation, reported on
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   the full dual-leg set and the CODE-overlap seat (the arena the
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   registered anomaly was detected on, step_123).
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   T3  signed dtp_io polarity: median sign inside the declared cap and
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   inside the mirror cap -- the bipolar slip field predicts
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   opposite polarities on the two lobes (step_089).
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   T4  timing-vs-geometry dissociation: |dtp_io| residualized against
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   (arc length, n_obs, leg-span asymmetry) -- a pure
[2026-09-21 15:43:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 159]   astrometric-noise floor should flatten the cap contrast.
